#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""sf1-hub-ben: Ben's per-person SF-1 hub runner, Linux / NixOS platform layer (2026-11-12, hub phase B, Ben's side).

This file is ONLY the platform layer: consent, kill switch, guard attach per checkout, systemd user unit, manifest.
The protocol lives in two shared pieces this file never re-implements:
  - the guard (oliver-ben-guard/guard.py, vendored byte-for-byte, sha in vendor.lock.json)
  - the shared hub runner core (sf1-v2/hub-runner/runner.py + deny_hook.py + room_member.py at branch
    sf1-hub-runner-oliver-1112 commit bb49e68c2, vendored byte-for-byte), the same bytes Oliver's macOS runner runs.
    hub_core_linux.py (platform layer, next to this file) runs it on Linux without editing it. If the shared prereg
    changes the protocol, re-vendor; never patch the vendored files.

Commands (no command prints or reads out a key):
  status                      what is installed, consented, attached, killed; no network
  token                       HUMAN ONLY: paste your private link; saves your own Sapience token (600), never printed
  attach <checkout> [--project <slug>] [--rules <source>] [--sink <sink>]
                              defaults (0.2.1): rules hub-route:https://app.spnc.ai/v1/projects/oliver-ben/rules,
                              sink hosted-events:https://app.spnc.ai/v1/rooms/<room>/events, key_file = your token
                              install the guard (attached mode) into ONE checkout: .git hooks + .claude/settings.local.json
  consent <checkout>          HUMAN ONLY (needs a real terminal): Ben types the consent phrase; writes the per-repo marker
  preflight                   the checks `serve` runs first; exit 0 = would start, 78 = refuses (systemd will not restart)
  serve                       preflight, then exec the shared runner core on the ONE consented card repo
  golive [--base <url>]       HUMAN ONLY: reads the room once; goes live only when the room shows the room thread's
                              verified go-live (its labeled SF-1 test post, then its digest message). Not verified:
                              refuses with no further call. Verified: the core's go-live (rules GET, mints Ben's key)
  kill                        kill switch: stop the runner and everything it started; no restart until `unkill`
  unkill                      HUMAN ONLY: remove the kill marker
  detach <checkout>           HUMAN ONLY: guard detach + restore that checkout's hook files byte-for-byte from the manifest
  uninstall                   HUMAN ONLY: kill, detach every checkout, remove every path in the manifest

Paths (XDG; nothing under /usr, nothing under ~/.claude):
  $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sf1-hub-ben/   env (token, mode 600, Ben writes it), KILL
  $XDG_STATE_HOME/sf1-hub-ben/    manifest.json, backups/, hub/ (the shared core's home: config, cards, worktrees,
                              log), repos.json (generated), serve.pid
  <checkout>/.git/oliver-ben-guard/CONSENT-<person>.json    the per-repo consent marker. It sits in the guard's own state
                              dir, so once `RULE guard-protect: all` binds, no attached Claude Code session can write it.
"""
